ISOLATED: factory calibration — legal opinion required before publication
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sources/LibreKit/Calibration/FactoryCalibration.swift converts raw sensor
values to mg/dL using the FRAM parameters i1–i6, a thermistor model and a
sensitivity grid. This conversion first appeared publicly in xdripswift
(GPL-3.0, 2020). The MIT-licensed projects that carry the same constants
(DiaBLE, GlucoseDirect, LibreTransmitter) cite xdripswift as their source,
so the MIT status of this piece is doubtful.

Glyph's file was written from a plain-language specification of the maths
(docs/factory-calibration.md), not copied: the 1 023-entry grid is generated
from its structure rather than reproduced. It is the only file that
implements the conversion and sits behind the GlucoseConverter protocol so it
can be replaced (for example by a fingerstick-based LinearCalibration).

Obtain a legal opinion on this file before the repository is made public.
